cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the SLR Workbench in a review or a paper, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the accompanying paper where a methods reference is appropriate."
type: software
title: "SLR Workbench"
abstract: "An offline, single-file workbench for conducting and reporting systematic literature reviews: attributable multi-database import, blocked fuzzy deduplication with a bounded edit distance, blinded dual-reviewer screening with Cohen's and Fleiss' kappa, PRISMA 2020 counts with consistency checks, the two-arm flow diagram, the 27-item checklist and an append-only audit log."
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/slr-workbench"
url: "https://USERNAME.github.io/slr-workbench/"
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.0000000   # add the Zenodo concept DOI once a release is archived
keywords:
  - systematic review
  - evidence synthesis
  - PRISMA 2020
  - deduplication
  - screening
  - inter-rater reliability
  - research software
authors:
